  "notes": "Strip is mostly estates, the cemetery, Mill Creek, the canal bed and railroads; only three crossings. Crawford Avenue left edge taken as the inner (pink-banded) lot line; an outer parallel line runs about 22 px east of it. Lafayette Avenue / McAlpin Avenue: the two streets merge at a sharp angle at the plate's left edge (block tip at about 160,6967); the centrelines have not quite met at x=0, so the pick at the edge is approximate and the true centre is probably just off the plate. Lafayette Avenue's outer edge in the bottom-left loop and along the left side is the plate cut, so its bends there are approximate. Spring Grove Avenue carries streetcar tracks and 10 in. and 30 in. water pipes; these are not street edges."
